This is the FGX C toolchain (fcc / fas / fgx_ld + the language runtime and
libc). It is original work; it includes no third-party source.

Some of fcc's design — notably the multibank far-pointer model and the
linker's bank-consistency behavior — was informed by studying the ORCA
development tools' source ("Opus ][: The Source", the ORCA/C compiler and
linker, Copyright (c) Byte Works, Inc. / Mike Westerfield). That source is
copyrighted and is NOT included or redistributed here: fcc ships independent
implementations of the *concepts*, never ORCA code. See
docs/decisions/orca-informed-decisions.md for the specific decisions and cites.

Should any third-party (e.g. 2.11BSD) source ever be ported into this tree, it
must carry an SPDX/FGX-Provenance header retaining the upstream copyright and be
listed in docs/PROVENANCE.md — same rule as the parent FGX repo. fcc's own code
is offered under the BSD-2-Clause license above.
